        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T18:08:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a bit concerned about the chance to receive and sign a partial write, or perhaps I\u0027m too paranoid. I was thinking maybe we can send the size first, followed by the whole data.  But then, an attacker can send anything anyway.  So a size prefix would only make it marginally more robust...  WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "f1a1fab44311cd7b9e54ab95c6fc6e3bc44095f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8688ea21_e7614058",
        "filename": "compos/compos_key_helper/compos_key_main.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-17T12:19:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If an attacker can invoke this binary and send anything to it, inside the VM with the trusted identity, then we already lost. So I don\u0027t think we need to defend against malicious truncation.\nFor accidentally  truncated input, that should never really happen - either the parent died (in which case the signature isn\u0027t going anywhere) or got a write error (which it deals with).\nSo I am fairly unworried about it.",
      "parentUuid": "52c106d0_ced6f2d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 23
      },
