      "writtenOn": "2022-02-17T12:19:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, this is my attempt. It is I think more obvious what it is doing, but there is some inherent inelegance.\nI also tested it, deliberately injecting faults, which revealed some missing selinux permissions (eg sigkill), and suboptimal logging.\n\nThis is all possibly academic, since the write_all seems to succeed even if the child exits immediately (buffered somewhere?). So I ended up just pretending it had failed.\n\nSample error logs (\"Foo\" is the pretend error from write_all):\n```\ncompsvc : compos_common::binder: Returning binder error: odrefresh failed\ncompsvc : \ncompsvc : Caused by:\ncompsvc :     0: Child exited: exit status: 0\ncompsvc :     1: Foo\n```\n\n```\ncomposd : composd_main::odrefresh_task: Running odrefresh failed: Status(-8, EX_SERVICE_SPECIFIC): \u0027-1: odrefresh failed\ncomposd : \ncomposd : Caused by:\ncomposd :     0: Child exited: signal: 9\ncomposd :     1: Foo\u0027\n\n```",
      "parentUuid": "5162562c_f8a6f37b",
